ng for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◇  \n[?25hMETA\nSEO Title: Bitcoin Selloff | Coinography Price Risk Breakdown\nMeta Description: See why Bitcoin slipped below $77K, how yields and oil pressure hit crypto, and which support levels traders should track next. Read now.\nURL Slug: bitcoin-selloff-below-77000-risk-assets\nCategories: Bitcoin News, Latest News\nPrimary Keyword: bitcoin selloff\nSecondary Keywords: crypto market pullback, BTC support level, Bitcoin liquidations\n\n# Bitcoin Selloff Pushes BTC Below $77,000 as Macro Stress Builds\n\nBitcoin selloff pressure intensified on May 18 as BTC traded near $76,900 and lost the $77,000 handle. Oil shock headlines and rising Treasury yields hit risk assets at the same time, pushing traders back into defense mode after a strong run.\n\nThe move was broad. SOL, DOGE, and XRP each fell about 5%, while crypto liquidations topped $563 million across the market. That shift quickly cooled momentum and forced traders to reassess short-term exposure.\n\nThis is not panic. It looks like a fast reset as leveraged longs unwind and macro risk takes priority.\n\n## Crypto market pullback: What This Bitcoin Selloff Signals\n\nThe first read is simple. [CoinDesk reported](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-under-usd77-000-as-oil-shock-and-treasury-yields-hit-risk-ass) that Bitcoin fell under $77,000 as higher yields and an oil shock weighed on risk assets. That points to a macro-driven move, not a crypto-specific failure.\n\nThe seasonal debate is back as well. [CoinTelegraph's analysis](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sell-in-may-historical-pattern-could-see-btc-back-at-33k-analyst?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound) said traders are revisiting the \"sell in May\" pattern because 2018 and 2022 both produced steep May drawdowns. [Google News aggregation](https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxQajIxZExWVjJnMXVteHdZVGVZZFNzbzlvZXVNSFFLaWR2Mm5HekNyVmxrUXpTX0lMMnJfMkJmV1FGdlcwN0U0YVF3U3ZUU2x0ZGhnSG1icE9aM0VSQkJVQldVYnpMN1I1YlhIUXVZTUlTd2NZN2h6VjZieUx5LTFwV0FtRVZQREFCVEZFWTYtU182TFZDTERFcmcySVZqRF9GalRBbXJTR0h2WVVnaHdJa2E2a0dNZ1dURnlpbVpxWERLZkI1?oc=5) showed the same pattern across multiple outlets, broad selling and heavy liquidations.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Macro pressure is driving this crypto market pullback\n\nThis drop fits the usual macro playbook. Higher yields tighten conditions, and oil-driven stress makes traders cut positions in high-beta assets first.\n\nThat matters because it frames the bitcoin selloff as a reaction to external pressure. When macro stress rises, crypto usually loses support faster because leverage and sentiment unwind together.\n\nJeff Ko made that distinction clearly. He argued prior May collapses were driven by specific shocks such as Mt. Gox fallout, China ICO restrictions, Fed tightening, and later Terra and FTX, not by the calendar itself. That means traders should judge this move through macro data and flow trends, not seasonality alone.\n\n- Oil shock headlines pushed traders into risk-off positioning.\n- Treasury yields rose and pressured speculative assets.\n- Forced liquidations accelerated once nearby support broke.\n\n### Why the historical comparison is not a clean repeat","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779089878470}}
